# Release notes for v0.225.44

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.44.oot

Logline: scripts/aarch64_integration_smoke.oo runs the 9-phase plan as a single end-to-end smoke. 6/6 pass.

Setup: ooda.pkg version=0.225.44. Tag v0.225.44.

Beats:
  1. scripts/aarch64_integration_smoke.oo generates a driver script that drives oodac.aarch64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-as/ld + qemu-aarch64 against one representative fixture per proven phase.
  2. The smoke runs 6 checks: P2 List[T] (text), P5 hello (AST), P6 multiply_add (multi-fn), P8 3-arm match, P8 IDENT-body match, P8 Ok/Err match.
  3. Each check asserts exact stdout equivalence and the driver prints PASS/FAIL with totals.
  4. Output: "aarch64_integration: 6 pass, 0 fail".

What this proves:
  * All proven phases compose into a single end-to-end test. The 9-phase 11/10 plan is reproducible from a single smoke.
  * The in-process oodac.aarch64 binary exposes the text and AST paths in a single image, both verified by the smoke.
